To explain briefly our reasoning: We want to devote our scarce resource of 8 drones to cover the highest threat fields fully. Field_1 has the highest threat (0.23) and is already near full coverage (3 protecting plus 1 en route) so we leave its four drones there. Field_3 comes next (0.15 threat) and needs only 2 drones for full protection. We take two drones from Field_2 (which, at 0.10 threat, is the least urgent despite having full protection at present) and reassign them to Field_3. That leaves Field_2 with two drones (so only partial protection, which is not as effective but still offers some benefit) and Field_4 remains unprotected because its threat is very low (0.07) and we cannot fully cover it with our available drones. This reallocation should help minimize overall damage.
